    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d535">

                <pb facs="0634" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg566"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/2654</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to President Wilson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 8, 1916</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: I enclose for your
                    consideration a suggested comment on the German reply, which, if you think
                    advisable, I might give to the press.</p>
                <p>In the event that we send a note to Gerard today, would you think it well to give
                    out the comment at the same time that we give out the text of our
                    instruction?</p>
                <p>In regard to the Commissioners for the Board of Investigation under our Treaty
                    with Great Britain,<anchor n="60" xml:id="d535-f1"/> I find that they are the following:<list>
                        <item>United States Commissioners— <list>
                                <item>Judge George Gray, of Delaware,</item>
                                <item>Mr. Domicio da Gama, <hi rendition="#italic">Brazilian
                                        Ambassador to the United States</hi>.</item>
                            </list>
                        </item>
                        <pb facs="0635" n="567" xml:id="pg567"/>
                        <item>British Commissioners— <list>
                                <item>Viscount James Bryce,</item>
                                <item>Mr. Maxim Koveleski, <hi rendition="#italic">Member of
                                        Counsel</hi> [<hi rendition="#italic">Council</hi>] <hi
                                        rendition="#italic">of Russian Empire</hi>.</item>
                            </list>
                        </item>
                        <item>Joint Commissioner— <list>
                                <item>Mr. Fridtjof Nansen, Norway.</item>
                            </list>
                        </item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d535-a1.xml" xpointer="d535-a1"/>
